  "title": "Fraction Word Problems: Smaller Recipes",
  "intro": "Explain scaling a recipe by referring to the original ingredient amount.",
  "html": "<h2>Teaching notes for parents and teachers</h2><h3>How to teach it</h3><p>Draw the amount needed for one recipe, then show half of that amount. Keep the measuring unit unchanged.</p><h3>Example to work through together</h3><p>Use the model below as you explain the example. Have your student point to the quantities as you discuss them.</p><div class=\"model recipe-cup-model\"><svg role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Three bars each represent one cup, divided into eight equal parts. A full cup is eight eighths, the recipe uses six eighths, and half the recipe uses three eighths.\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:600px\"><title>Keep one cup as the same whole</title><text x=\"20\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#164f5b\">One full cup</text><rect class=\"cup-row-0 selected-part\" x=\"20\" y=\"40\" width=\"45\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#176e5c\" stroke=\"#164f5b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect class=\"cup-row-0 selected-part\" x=\"65\" y=\"40\" width=\"45\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#176e5c\" stroke=\"#164f5b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect class=\"cup-row-0 selected-part\" x=\"110\" y=\"40\" width=\"45\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#176e5c\" stroke=\"#164f5b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect class=\"cup-row-0 selected-part\" x=\"155\" y=\"40\" width=\"45\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#176e5c\" stroke=\"#164f5b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect class=\"cup-row-0 selected-part\" x=\"200\" y=\"40\" width=\"45\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#176e5c\" stroke=\"#164f5b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect class=\"cup-row-0 selected-part\" x=\"245\" y=\"40\" width=\"45\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#176e5c\" stroke=\"#164f5b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect class=\"cup-row-0 selected-part\" x=\"290\" y=\"40\" width=\"45\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#176e5c\" stroke=\"#164f5b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect class=\"cup-row-0 selected-part\" x=\"335\" y=\"40\" width=\"45\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#176e5c\" stroke=\"#164f5b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#164f5b\">Recipe: 3/4 cup</text><rect class=\"cup-row-1 selected-part\" x=\"20\" y=\"130\" width=\"45\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#176e5c\" stroke=\"#164f5b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect class=\"cup-row-1 selected-part\" x=\"65\" y=\"130\" width=\"45\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#176e5c\" stroke=\"#164f5b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect class=\"cup-row-1 selected-part\" x=\"110\" y=\"130\" width=\"45\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#176e5c\" stroke=\"#164f5b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect class=\"cup-row-1 selected-part\" x=\"155\" y=\"130\" width=\"45\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#176e5c\" stroke=\"#164f5b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect class=\"cup-row-1 selected-part\" x=\"200\" y=\"130\" width=\"45\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#176e5c\" stroke=\"#164f5b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect class=\"cup-row-1 selected-part\" x=\"245\" y=\"130\" width=\"45\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#176e5c\" stroke=\"#164f5b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect class=\"cup-row-1\" x=\"290\" y=\"130\" width=\"45\" height=\"40\" fill=\"white\" stroke=\"#164f5b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect class=\"cup-row-1\" x=\"335\" y=\"130\" width=\"45\" height=\"40\" fill=\"white\" stroke=\"#164f5b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"210\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#164f5b\">Half recipe: 3/8 cup</text><rect class=\"cup-row-2 selected-part\" x=\"20\" y=\"220\" width=\"45\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#176e5c\" stroke=\"#164f5b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect class=\"cup-row-2 selected-part\" x=\"65\" y=\"220\" width=\"45\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#176e5c\" stroke=\"#164f5b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect class=\"cup-row-2 selected-part\" x=\"110\" y=\"220\" width=\"45\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#176e5c\" stroke=\"#164f5b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect class=\"cup-row-2\" x=\"155\" y=\"220\" width=\"45\" height=\"40\" fill=\"white\" stroke=\"#164f5b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect class=\"cup-row-2\" x=\"200\" y=\"220\" width=\"45\" height=\"40\" fill=\"white\" stroke=\"#164f5b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect class=\"cup-row-2\" x=\"245\" y=\"220\" width=\"45\" height=\"40\" fill=\"white\" stroke=\"#164f5b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect class=\"cup-row-2\" x=\"290\" y=\"220\" width=\"45\" height=\"40\" fill=\"white\" stroke=\"#164f5b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect class=\"cup-row-2\" x=\"335\" y=\"220\" width=\"45\" height=\"40\" fill=\"white\" stroke=\"#164f5b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/></svg><p>Each full bar represents one cup. Every small part is 1/8 of a cup. The whole does not change when the recipe gets smaller.</p></div><div class=\"model\"><p class=\"sample-equation\">3/4 × 1/2 = 3/8</p><p>Three fourths of a cup for a full recipe becomes three eighths of a cup for half the recipe.</p></div><h3>Ask your student</h3><blockquote><p>Are we finding half a cup or half of the amount in the recipe?</p></blockquote><h3>If your student needs help</h3><p>If the student always answers one-half cup, compare two recipes with different starting amounts.</p><h3>Choosing and using the worksheet</h3><p>Each set has four different recipe stories: two starting with less than one cup and two starting with more than one but less than two cups. Every multiplier is a proper fraction, and the original input denominators range from 2 to 8. Some fractions are not simplified, so students can practice equivalent forms without changing the original numbers.</p>",
